<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>agent-gate report</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body { font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif;
         margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 60rem; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  h1 { margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .meta { color: #666; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; }
  th { background: rgba(127,127,127,0.12); }
  caption { caption-side: top; text-align: left; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .rejected th { background: rgba(200,80,80,0.18); }
  .bar-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 0.2rem 0; }
  .bar-label { width: 11rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .bar-num { width: 3rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  svg .before { fill: #9aa7b1; }
  svg .after { fill: #3b82f6; }
  ul { margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  footer { color: #666; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .about { background: rgba(127,127,127,0.08); border-radius: 8px;
           padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .about h2 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .about p { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>agent-gate report</h1>
<p class="meta">
  Generated {{ data.generated_at }} &middot;
  agent model <code>{{ data.agent_model or "n/a" }}</code> &middot;
  judge model <code>{{ data.judge_model or "n/a" }}</code> &middot;
  first <code>{{ data.first_version or "n/a" }}</code> &middot;
  latest <code>{{ data.latest_version or "n/a" }}</code>
</p>

<section class="about">
  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>agent-gate</strong> is a regression gate for changes to an LLM
    agent's behavior. The agent is a fictional home services booking and
    dispatch assistant (HVAC, plumbing, electrical). Its behavior lives in
    versioned plain text policy files, and those files are the only thing that
    changes between versions.
  </p>
  <p>
    An improver LLM reads the current version's failures and proposes edits. A
    deterministic gate then accepts an edit only if it clearly improves a
    <em>dev</em> set, causes no confirmed regression in a protected
    <em>safeguard</em> set, holds on a hidden <em>holdout</em> set, and stays
    within cost and latency budgets. Every decision is written to disk with the
    numbers behind it. The improver never sees the holdout set.
  </p>
  <p>
    This page is one run's evidence. Section 1 compares the first policy to the
    latest on a frozen benchmark. Section 3, the rejected candidates table, is
    the point of the project: it shows the gate turning away bad edits, both
    ones the improver proposed and three deliberately bad policies written by
    hand to test it, with the exact rules they failed and the cases they
    regressed. Numbers are real and vary between runs because the model is non
    deterministic; the intervals and sample sizes are shown throughout.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
<table>
  <caption>1. Headline: first vs latest on the frozen benchmark</caption>
  <thead><tr>
    <th>Set</th><th>First</th><th>First passed/total</th><th>First 95% CI</th>
    <th>Latest</th><th>Latest passed/total</th><th>Latest 95% CI</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in data.headline %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ row.set_name }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.first.pass_rate | pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.first.attempts_passed }}/{{ row.first.attempts_total }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.first.ci95_low | pct }} to {{ row.first.ci95_high | pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.latest.pass_rate | pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.latest.attempts_passed }}/{{ row.latest.attempts_total }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.latest.ci95_low | pct }} to {{ row.latest.ci95_high | pct }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</section>

<section>
<table>
  <caption>2. Version history</caption>
  <thead><tr>
    <th>Version</th><th>Source</th><th>Dev</th><th>Safeguard</th><th>Holdout</th>
    <th>Mean cost/attempt</th><th>p95 latency</th><th>Decision</th><th>Reason</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for v in data.versions %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ v.version }}</td><td>{{ v.source }}</td>
      <td>{{ v.dev | pct }}</td><td>{{ v.safeguard | pct }}</td><td>{{ v.holdout | pct }}</td>
      <td>{{ v.mean_cost_usd | usd }}</td><td>{{ v.p95_latency_ms | ms }}</td>
      <td>{{ v.decision }}</td><td>{{ v.reason }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</section>

<section>
<table class="rejected">
  <caption>3. Rejected candidates (the most important table)</caption>
  <thead><tr>
    <th>Candidate</th><th>Source</th><th>Failed rule(s)</th><th>Regressed case ids</th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% if data.rejected %}
    {% for r in data.rejected %}
    <tr>
      <td>{{ r.candidate_id }}</td><td>{{ r.source }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.failed_rules | join(", ") }}</td>
      <td>{{ r.regressed_case_ids | join(", ") or "none" }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="4">No candidates were rejected.</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 style="font-size:1.1rem">4. Per category pass rates</h2>
  {% for c in data.categories %}
  <div class="bar-row">
    <span class="bar-label">{{ c.category }}</span>
    <svg width="320" height="30" role="img"
         aria-label="{{ c.category }} before {{ c.before | pct }}, after {{ c.after | pct }}">
      <rect class="before" x="0" y="2"  width="{{ (c.before * 300) | round(1) }}" height="10"></rect>
      <rect class="after"  x="0" y="16" width="{{ (c.after * 300) | round(1) }}" height="10"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span class="bar-num">{{ c.before | pct }}</span>
    <span class="bar-num">{{ c.after | pct }}</span>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <p class="meta">Top bar is before (first policy), bottom bar is after (latest policy).</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 style="font-size:1.1rem">5. Cost and latency</h2>
  <p>Total spend {{ data.cost.total_usd | usd }}{% if not data.cost.cost_known %} (pricing unknown, estimated){% endif %}.</p>
  {% if data.cost.components %}
  <table>
    <caption>Spend by component</caption>
    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Spend</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for comp in data.cost.components %}
      <tr><td>{{ comp.name }}</td><td>{{ comp.cost_usd | usd }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}
  {% if data.cost.per_version_latency %}
  <table>
    <caption>Latency per version</caption>
    <thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>p50</th><th>p95</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for lat in data.cost.per_version_latency %}
      <tr><td>{{ lat.version }}</td><td>{{ lat.p50_ms | ms }}</td><td>{{ lat.p95_ms | ms }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
<table>
  <caption>6. Flaky cases</caption>
  <thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Set</th><th>Passed/total</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% if data.flaky %}
    {% for f in data.flaky %}
    <tr><td>{{ f.case_id }}</td><td>{{ f.set_name }}</td><td>{{ f.passed_attempts }}/{{ f.total_attempts }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
    <tr><td colspan="3">No flaky cases in this run.</td></tr>
  {% endif %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 style="font-size:1.1rem">7. Limitations</h2>
  <ul>
  {% for item in data.limitations %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<footer>Static report, no JavaScript. Pass rates carry wide intervals at these sample sizes.</footer>
</body>
</html>
